module gunbc.spark.spark_gpu_direct_capability

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }

// ── WHICH PLATFORM THE CAPABILITY IS BEING ASKED ABOUT ────────────────────────────────────────
//
// THIS MODULE CARRIES A NAME AND NOT A READING, and the difference is the whole point. An earlier
// revision also carried the two `cuDeviceGetAttribute` outcomes as authored literals -- with the
// host, the driver revision and the date of the read in prose beside them -- and the live route
// consumed them as the authority deciding whether a staged collective memory path is a defect. That
// is a transcribed instrument output standing where its own producer already existed (DESIGN §6:
// name the instrument, never transcribe its output), and a declared frontier does not authorise the
// debt (DESIGN §5).
//
// THE READING NOW COMES FROM THE ROUTE. gunbc.spark.serving_rank_observe
// `observe_rank_gpu_direct_capability` runs `extdeps.nvidia.cuda_driver` `cuda_device_attribute_argv`
// inside the container the engine runs in and folds both replies through
// `extdeps.nvidia.gpu_direct_rdma` `gpu_direct_rdma_capability`, so the capability refreshes with
// the host it describes and a leg that cannot run yields Unread rather than a stale zero.
//
// WHAT IS STILL AUTHORED IS THE PLATFORM NAME, which is a fact about which hardware Group B IS
// rather than an answer any instrument returned, and it is what the Unsupported arm carries so a
// reader knows which device said no.
data spark_gb10_platform: NonEmptyStr = "NVIDIA GB10 Grace Blackwell (DGX Spark), unified LPDDR5X" as NonEmptyStr
